			"date": "2026-10-21T21:31:41.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Now I'm starting to double-guess if the original was even Access. I know the categories were all arbitrary and self-declared by each company registering, there was some effort to conform to pre-existing ones but it was a manual process.<br>Anyway, static sites can be arbitrarily awesome :-) and a good design process can trade processing for disk space well before the webserver itself gets involved!</p>",
