			},
			"date": "2026-10-21T22:17:22.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Oh boy, you want to know what I was doing back in 1995 then lol. We were operating an SSL website, which pins the date to 1995 as the earliest (therefore my other story needs to move forward a year I guess) and we had a 40-bit cert, one of the first to be deployed outside the US (small cert size because of export restrictions)<br>The website provided an actual catalog of things to buy from several different vendors, and collected ccard data for offline processing. Fun days!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
