			"url": "https://masto.hackers.town/@yojimbo/117481221007020388",
			"author": {
				"name": "CMDR Yojimbosan 🅅⁂",
				"url": "https://masto.hackers.town/@yojimbo",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/114/424/961/947/510/417/original/3fcff7080a46dcec.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2026-10-21T22:19:30.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Now, you don't want to know how we got the order and associated ccard from the web server to the customer, do you?<br>That was a little embarrassing, involving multiple emails with \"the first few digits\" on one message and \"the next few digits\" in another. And of course email wasn't encrypted.</p><p>In a spooky voice: \"This was before PCI existed and ... bad things happened ... on ... the Internet!!!!!\"</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
